  "worked_solution": "To find the second-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=\\operatorname{ln}\u20613,$ we plug $a=\\operatorname{ln}\u20613$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)+{f}^{\u2032}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)(x-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)+\\frac{1}{2}{f}^{\u2033}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613){(x-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out $f(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613),$ ${f}^{\u2032}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613),$ and ${f}^{\u2033}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{2x} & \u27f9 &  & f(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613) & =9 \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} & \u27f9 &  & {f}^{\u2032}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613) & =18 \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(x) & =4{e}^{2x} & \u27f9 &  & {f}^{\u2033}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613) & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now plug the results for $f(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613),$ ${f}^{\u2032}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613),$ and ${f}^{\u2033}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)$ into our second-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =9+18(x-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)+36\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{(x-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)}^{2} \\\\  & =9+18(x-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)+18{(x-\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
